          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Why does low iron make people tired?",
          "answer": "Low iron can lead to tiredness because iron is essential for making hemoglobin. Hemoglobin is a protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen throughout your body. When you don't have enough iron, your body can't produce enough hemoglobin. This results in fewer and smaller red blood cells that are less efficient at carrying oxygen to your tissues, leading to a feeling of tiredness. This information comes from the \"Iron-deficiency anemia\" document.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
